// Field reference: https://github.com/peterellisjones/dronecom-community/blob/main/data/docs/components.md
//
// Surface-class RWR spoofer (#5172) — the phantom-fleet payload. Radiates at
// 135 MW, the geometric mean of the two shipped surface search sets, so it sits
// symmetrically inside the 12 dB plausibility band for both: an_spy_310
// (300 MW) at -6.9 dB and an_sps_90 (60 MW) at +7.0 dB. The band is absolute,
// so over-radiating is caught exactly as under-radiating is.
//
// The 60 kW draw is what makes this a *surface* class, structurally rather than
// by declaration: it exceeds the largest air chassis's spare supply
// (`power_supply_kw - base_power_draw_kw`; the MQ-450's 29.0 kW is the ceiling)
// by 2.07x, so `Blueprint::validate` rejects it on every air hull with
// `OverPowerBudget`. That exclusion is asserted over the whole shipped chassis
// registry, so a new airframe is covered the moment it lands. It also excludes
// the USV-80 (45.0 kW spare): a 2500 kg boat has not got the generator to
// broadcast at ship-array power, so the phantom-destroyer play costs a real
// hull. A USV-80's deception play is the AN/ALQ-50 portraying an an_sps_90 —
// the lie its power plant can actually support.
//
// `emulates` is kept domain-coherent by authoring discipline, not by a sim
// rule: at 135 MW this class is within tolerance of every emitter on the
// ladder, including the airborne ones, and nothing in the sim would object to a
// USV squawking an AEW radar. Name surface sets only, and keep it that way.
//
// ORDER IS LIVE GAMEPLAY: the first entry is what this payload claims with no
// doctrine selection.
(
    id: "an_slq_80",
    designator: "AN/SLQ-80",
    codename: "Siren",
    category: Decoys,
    mount_rule: Single,
    weight: 150.0,
    // See the class-gate note above. Authored, never derived.
    power_draw: Fixed(60.0),
    // Unrestricted on purpose: the power budget does the excluding, which is
    // what the issue asks for. `[Domain(Sea)]` is the documented backstop if an
    // air chassis ever fields a 60 kW supply — nothing close exists today.
    allowed: [],
    payload: Decoy((
        channel: EmitterSpoofer(
            emulates: ["an_spy_310", "an_sps_90"],
            emission_strength: 135000000.0,
            mounting: MastEmitter,
        ),
    )),
)
